<div class="pschat" id="pschat"><h2>Ask PiShield</h2><p>Ask about your network in plain English. Choose what information the AI may read. Nothing here changes firewall or DNS rules.</p>
<div class="pschat-panel"><label>Local model <select id="psc-model"><option>Connecting…</option></select></label> <button id="psc-refresh" class="btn btn-default">Refresh connection</button> <button id="psc-reset" class="btn btn-default">New conversation</button><p id="psc-status" role="status">Loading…</p><div id="psc-tools"><strong>Data access for the next question</strong><div class="psc-toolrow"><label><input type="checkbox" value="report" checked> Latest report</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="devices"> Device activity</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="health"> System health</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="privacy"> Privacy counters</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="live"> Recent visible packets</label></div></div></div>
<div id="psc-history" class="pschat-panel" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="pschat-panel"><label for="psc-prompt">Your question or instruction</label><textarea id="psc-prompt" maxlength="1500" rows="3" placeholder="Is my TV sending tracking requests? Explain in plain English."></textarea><div class="psc-toolrow"><button id="psc-send" class="btn btn-primary">Send</button><button id="psc-propose" class="btn btn-default">Create a reusable tool</button><a href="pishield-ai?view=reports" class="btn btn-default">Saved AI reports</a></div><p>Reusable tools combine the approved read-only sources and your analysis instructions. Review before saving. No generated code runs.</p><div id="psc-proposal"></div><div id="psc-recipes"></div></div></div>
